23:Autism is a neurodevelopmental condition marked by impairments in social communication and interaction, alongside restricted and repetitive behaviors and sensory atypicalities 1 . It is still diagnosed based on behavioral observations and no validated biomarkers are available which could support diagnosis, strati /uniFB01 cation, or clinical management 2 . Efforts to identify replicable cognitive and biological substrates of the condition have been hampered by the pronounced biological, developmental, and clinical heterogeneity of individuals with autism 3 -7 . Standard case -control analytical approaches ignore such
